body:
Assuming `can_upload[idx]` doesn't get corrupted. I don't get how this could trigger:

1. `_fill_instance_data()` gets called.
2. Inside, `grow_instance_buffer()` gets called.
3. This will call `const bool must_remap = instance_buffer[p_render_list].prepare_for_map(p_append);`
    a. If `must_remap` returns true, then `map_raw_for_upload(0u)` will be called a few lines of codes later. The "must_remap" is literally the state of `can_upload[idx]`, so it can't fail.
    b. If `must_remap` returns false, then `map_raw_for_upload(0u)` should not be getting called. Perhaps we're here if `scene_state.curr_gpu_ptr[p_render_list]` was a nullptr. But how did we arrive to such state?

The only thing suspicious is that in _setup_render_pass_uniform_set, instance_buffer[p_render_list] creates an emergency buffer in case there was none, just to satisfy all validation:

```cpp
RD::Uniform u;
u.binding = 1;
u.uniform_type = RD::UNIFORM_TYPE_STORAGE_BUFFER_DYNAMIC;
if (scene_state.instance_buffer[p_render_list].get_size(0u) == 0u) {
	// < HERE: THIS BLOCK OF CODE CALLS CREATES AN EMERGENCY BUFFER AND CALLS prepare_for_upload()
	
	// Any buffer will do since its not used, so just create one.
	// We can't use scene_shader.default_vec4_xform_buffer because't it's not dynamic.
	scene_state.instance_buffer[p_render_list].set_size(0u, INSTANCE_DATA_BUFFER_MIN_SIZE * sizeof(SceneState::InstanceData), true);
	scene_state.instance_buffer[p_render_list].prepare_for_upload();
}
RID instance_buffer = scene_state.instance_buffer[p_render_list]._get(0u);
u.append_id(instance_buffer);
uniforms.push_back(u);
```

However `_setup_render_pass_uniform_set()` is called before `_fill_instance_data()`, not later. AND we call `prepare_for_upload()` in the emergency, so it should be fine.

I have no idea how we arrived to this invalid state.

